Appending <<<ServletContext>>> Manifests to the Registry

  On first use,
  {{{./apidocs-${project.version}/com/jcabi/manifests/Manifests.html}<<<Manifests>>>}}
  loads all <<<META-INF/MANIFEST.MF>>> files that
  {{{./apidocs-${project.version}/com/jcabi/manifests/ClasspathMfs.html}<<<ClasspathMfs>>>}}
  finds through the context
  {{{http://docs.oracle.com/javase/7/docs/api/java/lang/ClassLoader.html}<<<ClassLoader>>>}}
  of the current
  {{{http://docs.oracle.com/javase/7/docs/api/java/lang/Thread.html}<<<Thread>>>}}.
  This mechanism works just fine in web
  applications (<<<WAR>>> packages) as long as
  the current thread contains the same class loader as is being used in
  {{{http://docs.oracle.com/javaee/6/api/javax/servlet/ServletContext.html}<<<ServletContext>>>}}.
  In some web containers it is not true, and
  {{{./apidocs-${project.version}/com/jcabi/manifests/Manifests.html}<<<Manifests>>>}}
  simply won't see the <<<MANIFEST.MF>>> file of your <<<WAR>>> package.

  To solve the problem, append a
  {{{./apidocs-${project.version}/com/jcabi/manifests/ServletMfs.html}<<<ServletMfs>>>}}
  to the singleton registry, which reads <<</META-INF/MANIFEST.MF>>>
  straight from the <<<ServletContext>>>.
  Do it in one of your
  {{{http://docs.oracle.com/javaee/6/api/javax/servlet/ServletContextListener.html}<<<ServletContextListener>>>}}-s:

+--
public class MyListener implements ServletContextListener {
  @Override
  public void contextInitialized(ServletContextEvent event) {
    try {
      Manifests.singleton().append(
        new ServletMfs(event.getServletContext())
      );
    } catch (IOException ex) {
      throw new IllegalStateException(ex);
    }
  }
}
+--

  If your application uses <<<jakarta.servlet>>> instead of
  <<<javax.servlet>>>, use
  {{{./apidocs-${project.version}/com/jcabi/manifests/JakartaServletMfs.html}<<<JakartaServletMfs>>>}}
  instead of <<<ServletMfs>>>; it takes a
  <<<jakarta.servlet.ServletContext>>>.

  You can call
  {{{./apidocs-${project.version}/com/jcabi/manifests/Manifests.html}<<<append(Mfs)>>>}}
  many times, it's harmless for the registry.
